; The expression-grade coverage instrumenter, exposed as the dune
; instrumentation backend selected by
; --instrument-with ppx_windtrap.coverage.
;
; ONE library, naming ITSELF in (instrumentation.backend), exactly as
; ppx/mutate/dune does and argues at length: dune resolves
; --instrument-with <name> by reading the (instrumentation.backend) field
; of the library called <name>, and does not object to that field naming
; the library that carries it.
;
; The field deliberately does NOT hang off the ppx_windtrap library.
; That library's OTHER job is the inline-test rewriter, so it carries
; (ppx_runtime_libraries ppx_windtrap.runtime ppx_windtrap.config) — and
; dune adds a rewriter's ppx_runtime_libraries to everything it
; preprocesses, instrumentation included. A backend there would link the
; windtrap CORE into every instrumented library, which for lib/ — the
; core itself — is a dependency cycle
; (windtrap -> ppx_windtrap.runtime -> ppx_windtrap -> windtrap). That
; spelling shipped in 0.2.0 and is gone: one name, and it is the one
; that cannot drag the core in.
;
; The rewriter is also usable directly with
; (preprocess (pps ppx_windtrap.coverage)), which the semantics tests
; rely on. ppx_runtime_libraries makes every instrumented library link
; the windtrap.coverage runtime the generated code calls - and nothing
; else: instrumented user code must never pull the windtrap core into its
; closure.

(library
 (name windtrap_coverage_ppx)
 (public_name ppx_windtrap.coverage)
 (kind ppx_rewriter)
 (libraries ppxlib)
 (ppx_runtime_libraries windtrap.coverage)
 (instrumentation.backend
  (ppx ppx_windtrap.coverage))
 (preprocess
  (pps ppxlib.metaquot)))
